## Vendored third-party code

### tomlkit 0.13.3 — MIT

Vendored from its published PyPI wheel into `Source/vendor/tomlkit/` so that
round-trip edits to a user's TOML configuration preserve formatting and
comments.

- Upstream: https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit
- License: MIT — full text at `Source/vendor/tomlkit-LICENSE`
- Wheel SHA-256: `c89c649d79ee40629a9fda55f8ace8c6a1b42deb912b2a8fd8d942ddadb606b0`

`Source/codex_profile.py` inserts `Source/vendor` at the front of `sys.path`,
so the vendored copy is always the one that loads.

## Python dependencies

| Package | Status | License | Purpose |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `cryptography` 50.0.0 | required | Apache-2.0 OR BSD-3-Clause | Fernet sealing of stored reasoning envelopes (`Source/responses_bridge.py`) |
| `tomlkit` 0.13.3 | vendored | MIT | Comment-preserving TOML edits (`Source/codex_profile.py`) |
| `python-dotenv` | optional | BSD-3-Clause | Reading a Vibe-supplied `.env`; a built-in parser is used when absent |
| `certifi` | optional | MPL-2.0 | CA bundle for outbound TLS; falls back to the system trust store |

The two optional packages are imported inside `try`/`except ImportError`
blocks and degrade gracefully. Provider Hub runs without them.

`Source/requirements.txt` is the canonical runtime dependency list and is the
file named in the error shown when `cryptography` is missing from a runtime.
`pyproject.toml` mirrors it for development and CI.

## Provider logos

The images in `Source/provider-logos/` are third-party brand assets. Their
exact provenance — which came from TaskWraith and which from Limit Counter —
is recorded in `Source/provider-logos/README.md`. That file is the
authoritative attribution and ships alongside the assets.

Those images are **not** covered by the Apache-2.0 grant over the rest of this
repository. Copyright in each logo remains with the respective provider, and
they are reproduced here solely to identify which provider a route connects to.

If you redistribute this project you are responsible for complying with each
mark owner's brand guidelines, and for removing the assets if you cannot. Logo
paths are keyed by provider slug in `Source/provider_branding.json`, so removal
is a contained change.

